{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "RRULE test corpus for eventide recurrence support. Combines (a) RRULEs inferred from real Homzie user data, (b) RFC 5545 canonical examples, (c) Google Calendar / Apple Calendar emit patterns observed in the wild, (d) parser edge cases that historically break naive implementations. expected_first_occurrences is the oracle: any conformant RRULE parser (including the iOS EKRecurrenceRule builder and the Android CalendarContract.RRULE consumer) must, when given dtstart_utc and the rrule string, produce exactly these occurrence start times within the test_window. Where dateutil rejects an RRULE (e.g. Apple floating UNTIL), the field contains a \"_parser_note\" object explaining the parser disagreement that we want eventide to handle more gracefully than dateutil.",
  "test_window": {
    "start_utc": "2026-05-01T00:00:00+00:00",
    "end_utc": "2027-12-31T23:59:59+00:00"
  },
